    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:5a8704e80dc128a8",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "005357637ff72f42173bca9b8ae0b9ada02fcb98b0616ca7a03bd1724480a004",
      "text": "The Sirena Ranger Station lies in the heart of Corcovado National Park, a 50-minute boat ride from Drake Bay, with a wet landing on the beach: sandals are recommended. At the station, change into sturdier footwear to hike some of the park’s wildest terrain. Because Sirena is so remote, there is a greater chance of spotting some of the rarest rainforest wildlife: it rewards adventurous travellers with a true experience of what National Geographic has called “the most biologically intense place on Earth”. Overnight at Rancho Corcovado. (B, L, D)",
